## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-aware, tenant-scoped analytics with late-arriving data. Emphasizes incremental logic, governance, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental models with composite keys (tenant_id, date, event_type)
- Field-level redaction controlled by privacy_flag via a macro
- Late-arriving data handled through a short lookback MERGE
- Schema drift guards using sources, tests, and snapshots
- Exposures to reflect lineage in dashboards

## Code Example
```sql
-- macros/redact_email.sql
{% macro redact_email(email, privacy_flag) -%}
  {% if privacy_flag -%}
    {{ return('REDACTED') }}
  {% else -%}
    {{ return(email) }}
  {% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the redact_email macro across combinations of privacy_flag and null emails?
- How would you scale this approach to thousands of tenants with varying data freshness SLAs?

## Why This Matters
This interview question tests your understanding of macro correctness, multi-tenant schema templating, and CI/CD integration for data quality enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and singular/generic tests
- Per-tenant schemas using `analytics_{{tenant}}` naming convention
- CI gating: blocking deploys when any tenant's test reports NULL violations

## Code Example
```sql
-- analytics_base/macros/not_null_guard.sql
{% macro not_null_guard(tenant, model, col) %}
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM analytics_{{ tenant }}.{{ model }} WHERE {{ col }} IS NULL) = 0
{% endmacro %}
```

```sql
-- tests/generic/not_null_guard.sql
{% test not_null_guard(model, col) %}
  {% if execute %}
    {% set result = run_query(not_null_guard(this.name, model, col)) %}
    {% if result.rows[0][0] | int != 0 %}
      {% do exceptions.raise_compile_error(
        "Failed: " ~ model ~ "." ~ col ~ " contains NULL values"
      ) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endtest %}
```

The test verifies zero NULL values exist in the target column across all tenant-specific models.
